  "published": "2026-10-25T10:05:17.827Z",
  "readmeFile": "Readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2026-10-25\n\n - CTYQM001 flags the opening single quotation mark (U+2018), the single low-9 quotation mark (U+201A), and the single high-reversed-9 quotation mark (U+201B), in addition to the curly double quotes and guillemets it already flags.\n - The closing single quotation mark (U+2019) stays on CTYAP001 only.\n - Fix Typography Excludes so each pattern is its own glob. The default extension list, including an empty Excludes value, no longer registers those files as additional files.\n\n1.0.2 (2026-10-08)\n\n - A file already in Compile stays on the C# syntax tree and is not registered again as an AdditionalFile.\n - A .cs file that is not compiled is still an additional file when the globs match.\n - Package versions use the build number (1.0.N).\n\n1.0.0 (2026-09-19)\n\n - Initial release.\n - CTYED001 flags en dash (U+2013) and em dash (U+2014).\n - CTYQM001 flags typographic quotation marks (curly quotes and guillemets).\n - CTYAP001 flags typographic apostrophe / closing single quotation mark (U+2019).\n - CTYEL001 flags horizontal ellipsis (U+2026).\n - CTYMN001 flags minus sign (U+2212).\n - CTYNB001 flags no-break space (U+00A0) and narrow no-break space (U+202F).\n - ASCII hyphen, quotes, apostrophe, periods, and space stay silent.\n - Scans C# and matching extra files (Includes minus Excludes plus AdditionalExcludes).\n - Default severity is warning; set warning, error, message, or off per analyzer.",
